{{also|Jaffa}}
==English==

===Etymology===
From {{m|en|Jaffa}}, an ancient port city in Israel from which the oranges were exported. The sense "impotent male" is a reference to being "seedless"; see {{m|en|seed}}.
The cricketing sense, of a 'sweet ball' (from the bowler's perspective), is a metaphor further reinforced in Australian English where [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jaffas Jaffa] is also a trademark for a popular lolly that is red and round.

